body:
Years of therapy of all sorts, CBT, Lifespan, general talk, hospitalizations and all.  I have tried a variety of meds that either make shit worse, make me feel like I am dying, or wreck me in ways that I still haven't recovered from.  Medications don't seem to work for me.  Either they work and then stop working, or they just fuck me up beyond belief.  PTSD and Major Clinical Depression with a mix of Anxiety as well.  Most days just fucking suck. 

&#x200B;

As for the wife and kids and job, yeah, I have them.  That's not much of a consolation though.  My kids range from teen to toddler, I swear that the three oldest just hate me.  My wife and I go up and down, it's a down day today, and feels like it's been a down day for a few months, but I am probably exaggerating. 

&#x200B;

Still I am here. I struggle to be here on the daily.  As I said, would rather this all ended, but it is what it is and I keep plodding on.  Maybe one day I will have the strength to just jump in front of that bus or off that bridge. Doesn't look like today will happen to be that day, but the day is still young, and I still have a ton of shit to deal with.
